abstract = "Objective: To assess the reliability and validity of the revised version of 15 items of Taiwan version of Dangerousness Assessment(DA).Methods: On basis of expert review,a 15-item Taiwan version of DA was modified by adding five items.A convenient sample of 200 victims of intimate partner violence from Women' s Federation,the police station and other relevant agencies in Xinjiang and Hebei completed the Chinese pre-test version of DA and Brief Conflict Tactics Scale(BCTS).The total sample for item analysis,reliability,validity testing,and 50 victims were retested the DA after 2~4 weeks.Results: The items were omitted for its lower correlation and factor loading score by item analysis.The revised version of DA(DASR) consisted of two parts.The first part contained 9 items.The Cronbach coefficient of DA-R was 0.79.The item total correlations ranged from 0.29 to 0.66.The test-retest coefficients was 0.84(P0.01).Predictive validity ROC curve area under the curve(AUC) was 0.77,which reached moderate accuracy.The second part consisted of two items which used to determine the lethal behavior in the BCTS.This part did not court the scores.Conclusion: It suggests that the revised version of Dangerousness Assessment Scale(DAS-R) could be reliably used to assess dangerousness of intimate partner violence by the first-line staff in related fields.",
