abstract = "Abstract A one-group pretest-posttest design was used to investigate two fundamental research questions: (a) Do a significant number of students exhibit ethnic bias in their perceptions of the “typical” shoplifter; and (b) can we develop a classroom exercise with which educators can effectively increase students' awareness of such ethnic biases? A survey format coupled with a videotaped manipulation was used. Results revealed significant bias in participants' perceptions of likely retail shoplifters and provided evidence that the exercise implemented in the study successfully alerted students to the limitations of using ethnicity rather than behaviors as a predictor of retail shoplifting. Research implications and directions for future research are discussed.",
