pages = "19-26",
abstract = "An activist demonstration on company property can be extremely disruptive to normal business operations and cause a negative public relations situation. The role of the security/police department is critical in the control of this situation. The dilemma exists in the need to balance the right of free speech and assembly with the right of a company to conduct business. In order to manage a demonstration effectively, it is essential to have psychological knowledge of the purpose and stages of this action. Understanding the dynamics and functions of an activist group provides a security/law enforcement agency with an opportunity to prepare and manage the demonstration. This psychological knowledge will enhance security preparation and will increase the probability of a successful outcome.",
